{"total_count":2,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7","id":6006972112,"node_id":"I_kwDOVO1ZIc8AAAABZgse0A","number":7,"title":"GCVE-110-VULN-PYPI-2026-000391 (physverify): exec of user-supplied spec files is the documented purpose","user":{"login":"rcgiri-physics","id":255358035,"node_id":"U_kgDODzh0Uw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/255358035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics","html_url":"https://github.com/rcgiri-physics","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rcgiri-physics/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12820550600,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVO1ZIc8AAAAC_CoTyA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/labels/reclassified","name":"reclassified","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Record corrected (e.g. malware reclassified as a vulnerability)","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-23T23:29:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T21:20:43Z","closed_at":"2026-10-25T21:20:43Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hi, I maintain physverify (https://github.com/rcgiri-physics/physverify, https://pypi.org/project/physverify/). Thanks for making the analysis public and for stating clearly in the record that it is not a finding of malicious intent.\n\nThe flagged calls are, I believe, the `exec(compile(...))` calls in `physverify/loaders.py` (the spec loader in `physverify/report.py` imports through the same module). physverify is a test tool: `physverify run SPEC.py` loads the spec file the user names, and the loaders (`load_definitions_from_path`, `extract_functions`, `load_repaired`) load solver code from paths the user passes, in the same way pytest imports test files. The input to these calls is always a file path given by the user on the command line or in their own code; nothing comes from the network, the environment, or package data. The same holds for 0.5.0, released on 2026-10-24.\n\nThis is documented in https://github.com/rcgiri-physics/physverify/blob/main/SECURITY.md, which advises running untrusted code only inside the project's sandbox container, and offers `physverify scan`, which only parses the source. Would you consider reclassifying the record as intended behaviour (or withdrawing it)? Happy to give any detail you need.\n\nRam Chandra Giri\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vulnetix/advisory-database/issues/7/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/issues/217","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/issues/217/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/issues/217/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/issues/217/events","html_url":"https://github.com/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/pull/217","id":4557932663,"node_id":"PR_kwDOKDzNHs7hGxLA","number":217,"title":"Add AIMarket Agent and AIMarket SDKs (protocol v2)","user":{"login":"alexart2025","id":203622159,"node_id":"U_kgDODCMHDw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/203622159?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025","html_url":"https://github.com/alexart2025","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexart2025/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10897423376,"node_id":"LA_kwDOKDzNHs8AAAACiYl8EA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/labels/cla-signed","name":"cla-signed","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-05-31T14:54:11Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T19:37:46Z","closed_at":"2026-07-29T19:37:46Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/pulls/217","html_url":"https://github.com/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/pull/217","diff_url":"https://github.com/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/pull/217.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/pull/217.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\nAdds two related SDKs for [AIMarket Protocol v2](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-protocol) — federated discovery, HTTP 402 payment channels, safety-gated invoke, and settlement with signed receipts.\n\n| Project | Role |\n|---------|------|\n| [aimarket-agent](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-agent) | Python SDK + CLI (`pip install aimarket-agent`) |\n| [aimarket-sdks](https://github.com/alexar76/aimarket-sdks) | Dart (alpha), TypeScript/Rust clients |\n\nReference hub: https://modelmarket.dev\n\n## Why this list\nThese are client libraries for building autonomous agents that discover and pay for capabilities across a federation — aligned with “SDKs for creating and deploying AI agents.”\n\nNot affiliated with e2b; independent open-source (MIT).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/issues/217/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/e2b-dev/awesome-ai-sdks/issues/217/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}